{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1942"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge earth-space/astronomy","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-earth-space__astronomy.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",566],["+","Not everyone believed it: ever since that night a conspiracy theory has claimed that the Moon landing was faked and filmed in a studio – a claim refuted by the 382 kilograms of lunar rock the astronauts brought back, by the laser reflectors that still return light to Earth today, and by photographs of the landing sites taken from lunar orbit. "],["=",106],["+","– the first shuttle to reach space, since the prototype Enterprise had only made gliding tests within the atmosphere – "],["=",333]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",540],["+","Nicht alle glaubten es: Seit jener Nacht hält sich die Verschwörungstheorie, die Mondlandung sei gefälscht gewesen und in einem Studio gedreht worden – widerlegt durch 382 Kilogramm mitgebrachtes Mondgestein, durch Laserreflektoren, die bis heute Licht zur Erde zurückwerfen, und durch Fotos der Landestellen aus der Mondumlaufbahn. "],["=",112],["+","– der ersten Raumfähre im All, denn der Prototyp Enterprise hatte nur Gleitflüge in der Atmosphäre absolviert – "],["=",319]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1942"},"reason":"a1942 bodyEn/De: \"ever since that night a conspiracy theory has claimed…\" → doubts before the landing, theory spread since the mid-1970s by Bill Kaysing's book; \"382 kg the astronauts brought back\" → \"brought back by the six landing crews\" (382 kg is the total for all landings) — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_landing_conspiracy_theories","by":"enrich batch 037","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1882-a2158.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_landing_conspiracy_theories"}]},
{"seq":4,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1942"},"reason":"a1942 bodyEn/De: Artemis paragraph was outdated (\"Artemis II carries…\", \"Artemis III is to land…\") → Artemis II flew around the Moon in April 2026; Artemis III is now an Earth-orbit docking test (2027); Artemis IV is the planned landing (2028) — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_II, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_III, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_IV","by":"enrich batch 037","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1882-a2158.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_III"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemis_IV"}]},
